	- bars 7-8 and the matching bars of the second ending are marked Stop Time.
	- bars 10 and 12: three sixteenths are squeezed into the half beat after the eighth rest, typed as a sixteenth triplet (no 3 is printed).
	- bars 14-15 are hard to read in the scan, check the pitches and rhythm.
	- the sixteenth note run after the C7alt bar (bar 25 of the C part) and the run in the third bar of the coda are not legible in the scan, they are rests here. Put them in.
	- the F7 (funk) bars after the runs have a written bass figure under the slashes in the real book, only the slashes are here.
	- coda, second bar: a high eighth note with a flat at the end of the bar is not legible, it is a rest here.
	- the open solo on F7 is one repeated bar with a wavy line in the real book.
